---
import { withBase } from "../../lib/paths";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { cases } from "../../data/profile";
const item = cases.find((caseItem) => caseItem.slug === "ata")!;
---
<BaseLayout title="Agent Assurance — AI Agent Evaluation Platform" description="Agent Assurance, a record-first validation and regression layer for agentic systems, by Tran Quoc Truong.">
  <section class="border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] pb-16 pt-28 md:pb-24 md:pt-36">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
        <span class="rounded-md border border-sky-500/20 bg-sky-500/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-sky-700 dark:border-sky-400/30 dark:bg-sky-400/15 dark:text-sky-300">{item.label}</span>
        {item.period && <span class="tag">{item.period}</span>}
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-[var(--text-base)] mb-6 leading-tight max-w-4xl">{item.title}: {item.subtitle}</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[var(--text-muted)] max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-8">{item.summary}</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a class="btn-primary" href={withBase("projects/omni-agent/")}>View Omni-Agent</a>
        <a class="btn-secondary" href={withBase("projects/")}>Back to projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-24">
    <div class="case-study-shell">
      <article class="case-article">
        <section>
          <div class="mb-8 rounded-xl border border-sky-500/20 bg-sky-500/10 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-200">
            <strong class="text-sky-950 dark:text-white font-semibold">Award-winning Agent Assurance:</strong> The work was first recognized with 2nd Place at IVS Hackathon 2026, then presented as <strong>Flezi Polaris</strong> and received the <strong>Golden Solution Prize (1st place)</strong> at IVS Solution Day 2.0 on September 18, 2026. Its core capture, evaluation, and regression concepts are now integrated into Omni-Agent.
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Problem</h2>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-base)] mb-6">Traditional pass/fail testing does not explain agent behavior.</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">Agentic systems are probabilistic, multi-turn, and tool-using. A correct final answer does not prove that the agent used the right context, selected the right tools, handled intermediate failures safely, or behaved consistently across repeated runs.</p>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">Agent Assurance applies software-testing discipline to those systems by treating runtime execution as evidence, preserving it as durable records, and evaluating behavior against explicit requirements and scenarios.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Capture model</h2>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-base)] mb-6">Record first, then evaluate.</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">Execution evidence can be captured through LiteLLM or native OpenTelemetry paths. Multi-turn messages, tool calls, tool results, model responses, usage, and runtime metadata are reconstructed into normalized records before evaluation.</p>
          <pre class="bg-[var(--bg-subtle)] p-6 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] text-sm font-mono text-sky-800 dark:text-sky-300 overflow-x-auto mb-6">Agent execution
  → LiteLLM / OpenTelemetry capture
  → normalized trace records
  → behavioral evaluation
  → run-level assurance verdict</pre>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">Keeping capture separate from evaluation preserves raw evidence, makes regressions reproducible, and allows evaluation logic to evolve without changing the system under test.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Evaluation model</h2>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-base)] mb-6">Behavior is evaluated per record, not hidden inside an average.</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">Each record is evaluated across semantic behavior groups using a single evaluator workflow. The result retains evidence and rationale for each decision, and retries remain scoped to the affected group rather than re-running the entire evaluation.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-6">
            <li class="relative pl-6 before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-2.5 before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-sky-500">Missing or insufficient evidence produces an <strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">inconclusive</strong> result instead of a guessed score.</li>
            <li class="relative pl-6 before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-2.5 before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-sky-500">Run-level behavior uses <strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">worst-record aggregation</strong>, so a decisive failure cannot be hidden by strong averages elsewhere.</li>
            <li class="relative pl-6 before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-2.5 before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-sky-500">The decisive record is retained and surfaced so a verdict is auditable rather than opaque.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Reproducibility</h2>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-base)] mb-6">Requirements and scenarios are versioned with the run.</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">Assurance runs depend on explicit requirement and scenario versions. Editing the source definition creates a new version, while completed runs retain the exact snapshots they were evaluated against. This avoids historical drift and makes regression comparison meaningful.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Architecture</h2>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-base)] mb-6">Thin control plane, asynchronous evaluation, durable evidence.</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-6">
            <li class="relative pl-6 before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-2.5 before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-sky-500"><strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">FastAPI API</strong> — project-scoped assurance configuration, run lifecycle, and reporting.</li>
            <li class="relative pl-6 before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-2.5 before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-sky-500"><strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">Celery + Redis</strong> — asynchronous trace finalization and evaluation work.</li>
            <li class="relative pl-6 before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-2.5 before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-sky-500"><strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">PostgreSQL</strong> — durable requirements, scenarios, execution records, evaluation results, and version snapshots.</li>
            <li class="relative pl-6 before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-2.5 before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-sky-500"><strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">LiteLLM + OpenTelemetry</strong> — complementary runtime capture paths for model traffic and native agent traces.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Maturity</h2>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-base)] mb-6">Validated through two internal competitions; evolving as part of Omni-Agent.</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">The standalone project proved the core evidence-capture and evaluation model and was recognized at both IVS Hackathon 2026 and IVS Solution Day 2.0. The current direction is a project-centric assurance capability inside Omni-Agent, with explicit requirements, scenarios, reproducible runs, and operational reporting.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Stack</h2>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-4">
            {item.tags.map((tag) => <span class="tag">{tag}</span>)}
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>

      <aside class="case-aside">
        <div class="evidence-card">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Role</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">{item.role}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence-card">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Evidence</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">{item.outcome}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence-card">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">Current model</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">Unit:</strong> recorded agent execution evidence</p>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">Aggregation:</strong> worst-record behavior gate</p>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-[var(--text-base)]">Reproducibility:</strong> versioned requirements and scenarios</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>